# Performance

## Purpose

Guard latency and jank on hot paths without duplicating caching mechanics.

## When Applied

Request for perf work, or when changing lists/dashboards/streams/queries. Complements [`../data/caching-sync.mdc`](../data/caching-sync.mdc).

## Requirements

- Keep cache-first reads; avoid awaiting cache writes on the UI path (`unawaited(...)`).
- Select only needed columns; avoid N+1 client round-trips — push joins/aggregation into RPCs/views.
- Scope rebuilds: `buildWhen`/`Equatable`, `const` widgets, keys on long lists.
- Use `shimmer_widgets` placeholders instead of blocking spinners on first paint.

## Examples

- Dashboard summary → one RPC/view call, not several sequential `.from(...)` reads.

## Anti-patterns

- Fetching a full table then filtering in Dart.
- A `BlocBuilder` that rebuilds a whole page on every unrelated state change.

## Common Mistakes

- Missing `buildWhen`, causing wasteful rebuilds.
- Synchronous cache writes adding latency to navigation.
